```java
public class Test {
    int classVar = 10; // Can be used anywhere in class

    public void myMethod() {
        int localVar = 5; // Only exists in myMethod
        if (true) {
            int blockVar = 3; // Only exists in this if block
        }
    }
}
```

• Variables must be declared before use
• They only exist within their scope
• Trying to use a variable outside its scope causes errors

examples:
public static void main(String[] args) {
    int x = 10;  // x is in scope for entire main

    if (x > 5) {
        int y = 20;  // y is only in scope inside this block
        System.out.println(x + y);  // OK: both visible
    }
    // System.out.println(y);  // Error: y is out of scope
}
